# Line endings.
#
# Git stores text as LF and, with core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default), checks it out as
# CRLF. Prettier's endOfLine defaults to "lf", so on Windows a *clean checkout* failed
# `npm run lint` with 19,132 "Delete ␍" errors before anyone had edited anything — while
# `git status` stayed clean, because the normalisation happens on commit. CI never saw it: it
# runs on Linux, where the checkout is LF anyway.
#
# Pinning eol=lf makes every platform check out what the tooling expects. This overrides
# core.autocrlf, so no one has to change their global git config.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Except Windows batch files: some Windows shells mis-parse an LF-only .bat, and gradlew.bat is
# the documented way to build on Windows.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binaries must never be touched. `text=auto` detects most of these on its own; naming them is
# cheaper than finding out it guessed wrong about a font or a keystore.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.svg text eol=lf
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.jar binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
*.apk binary
*.aab binary
*.so binary
*.pdf binary
